cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Laconic in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "Laconic: token-efficient middleware for multi-agent LLM workflows"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Laconic contributors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-02
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/lindameng-0/laconic"
abstract: >-
  Laconic compresses the natural-language payload of inter-agent messages in
  multi-agent LLM workflows while preserving structural scaffolding (tool
  calls, arguments, identifiers, schemas) losslessly. It operates entirely in
  the text channel, targets closed models accessed via API, measures all
  savings with the target model's tokenizer, and includes a reproducible
  benchmark harness characterizing cross-model compression tolerance of agent
  traffic.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - multi-agent systems
  - prompt compression
  - token efficiency
